1
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:26,840
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River

2
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too

3
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:42,300
onto the head of the carpenter I was choking

4
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed that I was still just a brat

5
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,
there's still hope in Katsushika

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,540
With a yawn, the unchanged
streetscape feels strangely gentle

7
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:14,640
from the pointed-hat water
bottle up to the vast sky

8
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,780
The sun sets

9
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow too, it'll end just like this, huh

10
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,040
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness again

11
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,760
I only realized it after losing it

12
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,860
Because I'm such a fool

13
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,740
Here it is, Komachi-chan.

14
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:50,960
Check the contents.

15
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:51,620
Yeah.

16
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:59,740
Is that Komachi-chan's boyfriend?

17
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:02,040
He's quite a handsome guy, isn't he?

18
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,180
No, it's not like that, Uncle.

19
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:07,200
Nakagawa-san.

20
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:17,140
Where was this taken?
It looks like a really nice place.

21
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:20,280
It's my hometown.
There's really nothing there.

22
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:25,520
So that rugged country guy is
in the photo with Komatsu-chan

23
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:33,440
Whoa, I forgot. He came along too.

24
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,540
You two

25
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,460
Don't tell me you went that far

26
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,120
What are you talking about, Dad?

27
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,940
Ryotsu-san

28
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:00,640
She's an unworthy daughter,

29
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:02,800
but please take good care
of her for years to come.

30
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:06,060
Whoa! That's totally awesome!

31
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:11,140
If everyone sees a photo like this,
my credibility is going to plummet!

32
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:13,500
W-what do I do...

33
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,100
Wow! Everyone, look!

34
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:23,420
What? What? What happened?
What happened? What happened?

35
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:26,860
Just look at this.

36
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:30,880
It's a two-shot of Komachi and Nakagawa-san!

37
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:34,040
No way.

38
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:36,200
Yay, yay, yay!

39
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,420
Yay, yay, yay!

40
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:40,160
Whoa!

41
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:40,960
Hey.

42
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,120
Komachi, what's going on?

43
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:46,540
I took it when I went back home
during summer vacation.

44
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:49,000
With Nakagawa-san.

45
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,260
Don't tell me you two were alone together?

46
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:04,460
So many two-shots with Nakagawa!

47
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:10,740
Komachi, when you bring your boyfriend home to meet the family,
things must be pretty serious between you two, right?

48
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,520
Come on, own up to it!

49
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,140
It's not like that at all.

50
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:22,120
There was a marriage arranged meeting at my parents' place,
so I brought in Nakagawa to turn it down.

51
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:24,460
So you summoned him as your boyfriend?

52
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:26,580
No way... I'm shocked.

53
00:04:27,860 --> 00:04:29,380
So that means he really is...

54
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:29,640
Then...

55
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:32,180
That's not fair! Not fair at all!

56
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,220
I'm so jealous! Absolutely jealous!

57
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,400
I could kill you!

58
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,700
Unfair!

59
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,020
Well so...

60
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,500
Hello, Traffic Division.

61
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:46,720
Mom.

62
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,240
Yeah, it's me.

63
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,320
You're coming to Tokyo?

64
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,160
Yeah, this Sunday, the day after tomorrow.

65
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:57,240
So, how are things going
with that boyfriend of yours?

66
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:58,360
That boyfriend?

67
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:01,320
Nakagawa-san is totally out of the question.

68
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,660
We're talking about Nakagawa-san.

69
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:05,460
Yeah, yeah, it's about Ryo-san.

70
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,760
Wait, Mom, don't get the wrong idea.

71
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:15,240
Oh no, everyone thinks
it's about Nakagawa-san.

72
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:18,860
I wouldn't say that caveman's name
even if my mouth was torn open.

73
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,980
I was talking with Dad about it too,
you know.

74
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:23,880
He's quite a manly guy and a nice person,
isn't he?

75
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:27,380
So I'm not that close with him.

76
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:38,480
Up to your worthless tricks again,
you two, Komachi and Naoko.

77
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,363
Well, seeing how close you two are,

78
00:05:41,413 --> 00:05:45,900
I think it's about time you took
things all the way to marriage.

79
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,840
Marriage!?

80
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:49,660
Eeeeeeeh!?

81
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:51,620
Marriage, you say!?

82
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:54,360
That's not fair!
Hogging Nakagawa-san all to yourself!

83
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,020
Isn't that still too early, I mean?

84
00:05:58,020 --> 00:05:59,160
As for us,

85
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,380
Well, the phone bill will get expensive, so

86
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:02,720
Say hello to Ryo-san for me.

87
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:04,720
Mom

88
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:09,200
You're so impatient.

89
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:15,340
I've been waiting for you.

90
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:19,420
What are you doing here, caveman?

91
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:22,760
Do I look like a stray dog to you?

92
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:36,880
Podoi is number one for most hated, number one for man you don't want to marry, number one for man you don't want as a lover,
number one for man you don't want to date, number one for man you don't want to be photographed with.

93
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:40,840
So what are you here for?
All of you singing together like that!

94
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:48,100
I came to complain about this.
Don't go poking your nose into things.

95
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,940
Wasn't that guy...

96
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,900
When I went to Komachi's countryside

97
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:55,640
Whoa!

98
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,360
What, what's going on here?

99
00:06:58,580 --> 00:06:58,980
I see.

100
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,380
So you cropped the panoramic photo

101
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:10,060
Every part where I appear
has been cleverly cut out.

102
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:14,340
Without me in it,
I guess it does look like a couple's trip.

103
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:14,860
Right?

104
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:18,620
The atmosphere's such that we
can't now say you were with us.

105
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,900
Yeah, well, it's none of my concern.

106
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:25,500
After that newspaper article,
nobody's going to cooperate!

107
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:28,520
That's why I'm asking you
to do something about it.

108
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:29,520
Please?

109
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:31,520
No way.

110
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:32,480
What?

111
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:36,340
I'd like to say that,
but I'll be generous and let it slide.

112
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:41,880
I'll settle for a retraction of this
article and an apology printed in the paper.

113
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,280
If you don't want to, that's fine.

114
00:07:45,850 --> 00:07:50,400
If you just ask Nakagawa or Reiko to keep quiet,
they'll do it, you know.

115
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:54,640
But my mouth is incredibly loose, you know.

116
00:07:55,190 --> 00:07:56,320
Ugh...

117
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,960
Fine, fine, I'll do it.

118
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,500
Right now! Show me the goods!

119
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:05,200
I said fine, didn't I?

120
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,080
Then it's a total secret, got it!

121
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:12,700
You're naive.

122
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:18,280
Photos from when Komachi-chan went to her hometown over summer break?
I have them.

123
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,560
But you've already seen them before, senpai.

124
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:23,740
I was thinking you'd make
me some yaki-mashi too.

125
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:27,020
But you said you didn't want any back then.

126
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:29,100
Here you go.

127
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,500
No, I've changed my mind.

128
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:37,040
This is it, this is it!

129
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:38,540
It's splitting apart!

130
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:43,060
What's the meaning of this?

131
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,540
Apology and Correction

132
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:49,900
There was a tallying error in the
"most hated" survey we published in this month's issue.

133
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:54,000
Sakonji Tatsunosuke moves up to first place.

134
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,440
How could this be?

135
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:59,020
Why does it have to be me?

136
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:03,380
I thought we'd be safe as
long as Ryotsu was around.

137
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:07,380
Damn it! Women, my ass!

138
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:12,060
I'm going into the mountains to train
for the upcoming martial arts tournament!

139
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:22,080
What's with women! What's with women!

140
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:24,260
I've got Saori!

141
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:25,880
Saori!

142
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,920
Hey, Komachi, what's going on?

143
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:36,440
That's right, that's right.
There was no mistake in the tally!

144
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:39,740
That caveman was number one by a landslide!

145
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:42,780
Is that so? Well, whatever.

146
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:45,960
I mean, if you're always together,
there's no freshness.

147
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:47,360
But, you know...

148
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:48,880
Hey, Komachi.

149
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:50,900
What are you doing here again?

150
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:53,820
Shut up, I've got business with Komachi.

151
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:57,260
Hey, Komachi, I forgot my wallet.

152
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:58,980
Could you lend me about 30,000 yen?

153
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:00,720
What did you say?

154
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:03,760
Get lost, get lost, you slimy freeloader.

155
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,020
I told you, I forgot my wallet.

156
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:06,920
Right, right.

157
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,800
I hear you're totally
lovey-dovey with Nakagawa.

158
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:14,660
You went all the way to your hometown with him,
just the two of you,

159
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:16,600
and introduced him to your parents, right?

160
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,240
Just the two of you?

161
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:23,500
Damn it.

162
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:25,860
So you got it from Reiko-san this guy.

163
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,380
F-fine, I get it.

164
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:29,940
Thirty thousand yen, is that enough?

165
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,480
Wow, you're so understanding.

166
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:37,520
Then I'll borrow it.

167
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:41,160
And you said I can pay it back whenever.

168
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:43,700
Really? Thanks.

169
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:43,940
Hey.

170
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:48,660
What on earth is going on?

171
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:49,960
That's not like you, Komachi.

172
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:50,440
Seriously.

173
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:52,280
It's nothing!

174
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:54,240
It's more like,
"Don't mind it, don't mind it."

175
00:10:58,940 --> 00:10:59,940
What's going on?

176
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,300
Ryo-san,

177
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:05,480
the mini-patrol cars have taken
over all the parking spaces,

178
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:08,420
so we can't park our patrol cars.
We're in a real bind.

179
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:14,520
That's because when we go to protest,
they fire back ferociously.

180
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:16,940
Komachi's especially fierce.

181
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:20,600
Are you scared of that? How pathetic.

182
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,260
So Ryo-san's fine with it?

183
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:29,220
Leave all of that to me.

184
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,820
Nothing is impossible for me.

185
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,660
Our savior!

186
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,540
Please, Lord Ryo.

187
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:41,400
Please help us. Could you tell
the mini-patrol to park out back?

188
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:45,040
Is that all?
Don't you have anything else to say to them?

189
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,680
Abolish the station-wide smoking ban.

190
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,620
Hand out the Valentine's chocolates fairly.

191
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:55,480
Look at people's faces and laugh.

192
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:59,180
Fine, fine,
I'll take care of all of you at once.

193
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:04,140
But it's 10,000 yen for every
demand I get accepted, got it?

194
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:07,700
What did you say?

195
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:11,100
They say the mini-patrols are in the way,
so park them out back.

196
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,860
There's no way that could be allowed.

197
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:18,000
Can you afford to be so tough, Komachi-chan?

198
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:24,200
Apparently you're lovey-dovey with Nakagawa.

199
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:27,100
What are you talking about?
It has nothing to do with you.

200
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:30,380
Is that so, Komachi-chan?

201
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:35,300
Fine, fine, I admit it.

202
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,600
Komachi, what are you saying?

203
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:41,020
That's the spirit!

204
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:44,920
And also, abolish the total
smoking ban inside the station,

205
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:48,340
and I demand that Valentine's
chocolates be distributed fairly. Got it?

206
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:50,980
Fine.

207
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:54,200
Komachi really is understanding, isn't she?

208
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:58,080
Looks like we'll get
along just fine from now on.

209
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,260
Take care of me, then.

210
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:04,120
Oops, my geta got dirty.

211
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:06,060
Hey, Komachi.

212
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:13,160
Well, let's really wipe it clean nicely.

213
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,560
Yes, yes, you're so thoughtful.

214
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:19,960
We're always being
pushed around by this guy.

215
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:21,980
Let's keep tormenting him from now on.

216
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:25,360
At this rate,
we'll be made fools of by this caveman.

217
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,900
We have to do something.

218
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:41,320
Ryo-chan said that?

219
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:42,940
That's really awful, isn't it.

220
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:46,260
As soon as he hears the word
"secret," he turns into a devil.

221
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,660
If this goes on, he'll do whatever he wants.

222
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:51,600
I'm in trouble, what should I do?

223
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:54,620
So, what I mean is, a photo of just
the two of us, you and Kei-chan,

224
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,480
is what we need, right?

225
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:00,400
Hey, but if Nakagawa-san
finds out about this,

226
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:06,580
don't worry. I'll talk to Kei-chan
properly and take a two-shot photo for you.

227
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:12,360
Really? Thank goodness. Leave it to me.

228
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:29,480
Anyway, you didn't say that your
senior would tag along, did you?

229
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:33,260
I told them that Kei-chan would
show a friend from France around.

230
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:35,840
Ryo-chan said he'd rather stay in
his room building his model kits.

231
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,780
I see, you really thought that through.

232
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:40,100
That flower clock is really pretty.

233
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:41,800
Let's take a picture.

234
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:44,100
Is this all right?

235
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:50,520
Did you really think you could
fool me with such a cheap trick?

236
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:54,120
Reiko, I saw through your
scheme from the flowers onward.

237
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:57,040
Could you two stand a
little closer together?

238
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:58,500
That'll make a better picture.

239
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:01,540
Really? Like this?

240
00:15:02,220 --> 00:15:02,960
Okay, here we go.

241
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,580
Say cheese!

242
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:07,537
Oh my,

243
00:15:07,587 --> 00:15:11,040
Was that something I just saw,
or is it an optical illusion?

244
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:20,660
Okay, let's take the next
one in front of the dinosaur.

245
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,240
Komatsu-chan, a bit more to the right.

246
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,380
Alright, here we go, I'm taking it!

247
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:27,300
Say cheese!

248
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:32,160
Was that Ryo-chan just now?
No way, surely not.

249
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,820
Even the haunted house, too...

250
00:15:38,340 --> 00:15:39,900
Yep, it was Ryo-chan.

251
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,060
Come here for a moment, Komachi-chan.

252
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:46,160
This is bad, Ryo-chan is getting in the way.

253
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:46,600
What?

254
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:51,320
He's in every single
photo we've taken so far.

255
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,780
No way...

256
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,740
What is it? Did something happen?

257
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:59,389
N-no, it's nothing.

258
00:15:59,439 --> 00:16:02,160
I wonder where we should go next

259
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:07,660
If we're on the river,
Ryo-chan can't interrupt us.

260
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:10,420
Hey, let's ride that gondola. Okay?

261
00:16:11,500 --> 00:16:13,920
Sounds good, let's ride it. Right, right?

262
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:16,900
Come on, Kei-chan, hurry, hurry.

263
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:17,280
Ugh.

264
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,400
Damn, this guy's noticed us.

265
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,760
No way I'm letting that happen.

266
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:28,760
We've got a really nice atmosphere,
don't we.

267
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,520
One photo, please.

268
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,120
Okay, I'm taking it.

269
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,620
Say cheese!

270
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:36,540
Whoa, what the -

271
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:40,300
Snuggle, snuggle, snuggle.

272
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:47,580
It tipped over!

273
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:48,200
What happened?

274
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:54,920
A kappa!

275
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,040
The kappa did it!

276
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:56,800
It's over there!

277
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:58,980
Reiko-san says it's a kappa.

278
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:02,080
This is Ryo-chan's doing, isn't it.

279
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:03,660
If it's come to this...

280
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:09,000
Why are you two in such a hurry?

281
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:12,980
I won't let him get in the way,
no matter what!

282
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:20,340
Don't think you can escape from me!

283
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:23,360
Hey, Reiko!

284
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:27,720
The onigiri!

285
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,720
Ow

286
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:36,760
Damn it!

287
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:42,620
Looks like we shook him off.

288
00:17:42,620 --> 00:17:45,040
If it starts moving now, we'll be fine.

289
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:50,940
Crap, it's already left?

290
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,540
Isn't there some way to stop him?

291
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:01,400
There it is.

292
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:06,520
We're safe now that we've come this far.

293
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,540
Just a little more.

294
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:17,040
Now!

295
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:24,400
S-senpai fell from the sky!

296
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,680
This is the worst.

297
00:18:26,150 --> 00:18:28,060
Ryo-chan,
stop getting in the way all the time!

298
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:30,680
Not a chance. Hand over the camera!

299
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:31,500
No way.

300
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,100
Hand it over, you fool!

301
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:33,900
That's amazing.

302
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:39,260
Yay, look at me getting in the way!

303
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,800
Yo-chan.

304
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:55,460
Quick, while Ryo-chan isn't here!

305
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:57,040
Reiko-san, what's going on?

306
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:00,040
Kei-chan doesn't need to worry about it.

307
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:00,240
But...

308
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:02,900
Okay, I'm taking it. Say cheese!

309
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:06,080
Whoa, senpai, since when were you here?

310
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,340
Heh, too bad!

311
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:10,100
Got one!

312
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:13,720
Okay, I'm taking it.

313
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:15,740
Mm, not yet, not yet.

314
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:18,580
Aaaaaah!

315
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:21,980
How about here?

316
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,900
Say cheese!

317
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:26,140
Nice try, but too naive!

318
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:27,720
Darn it!

319
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:32,300
Aaaaah!

320
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:39,220
Aaaaah! Aah!

321
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:45,740
Purikura! This one definitely won't show Ryo-chan!
I'll keep watch, so hurry, hurry!

322
00:19:45,740 --> 00:19:46,900
Okay!

323
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:56,580
It's fine.

324
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:58,920
Ryo-chan isn't in sight.

325
00:19:58,920 --> 00:19:59,600
Yes!

326
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:00,820
We finally got it, didn't we?

327
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,320
What is this?

328
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,320
What's going on?

329
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:44,440
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

330
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:52,660
Oh no, the 500-yen coin!

331
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:54,380
Where, where is it?

332
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:55,960
Wait!

333
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,440
Now, Ken-chan and Komachi-chan!

334
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:12,460
Yes!

335
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:17,360
Too bad.

336
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:19,340
I win, Ryo-chan.

337
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:22,420
It's not like I have to do
whatever you say anymore, right?

338
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:25,580
Damn it, all our efforts until now...

339
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:31,940
Then, please do this one.

340
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:35,020
Sure, it'll be ready by tomorrow morning.

341
00:21:39,020 --> 00:21:40,980
If it's come to this,
I'll see it through to the end.

342
00:21:40,980 --> 00:21:44,160
There's no such word as
"defeat" in my dictionary!

343
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:56,400
Found it, found it! This one!

344
00:21:57,140 --> 00:22:00,420
Game over, you lost!
There's no way you can beat me!

345
00:22:02,220 --> 00:22:05,340
We just got here,
where are you taking us, Komachi?

346
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:08,120
Just follow me, Mom.

347
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:10,700
Honestly,
you've got it totally wrong, I mean...

348
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:12,700
I'll show you the proof so there's no doubt.

349
00:22:14,420 --> 00:22:15,460
Here, it's all set.

350
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:20,400
Come on, Mom,
look at this and you'll see clearly.

351
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:28,540
See? You understand now, right?

352
00:22:28,540 --> 00:22:30,240
My boyfriend is this guy.

353
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:33,400
This girl, going to all this trouble...

354
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,960
I knew it, it's Ryo-chan, isn't it!

355
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:38,080
Yes, my boyfriend is Ryo-san.

356
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:41,420
Mom, where are you looking?!

357
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:52,580
That guy!

358
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:57,640
Hey, you caveman!

359
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,080
Serves you right, look at that!

360
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:02,880
How did my special photo turn out?

361
00:23:05,980 --> 00:23:06,780
Aaaaaah!

362
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:07,340
Aaaaaah!

363
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:14,980
Do you want everyone to find out
the photo of you and Nakagawa is fake?

364
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:16,380
Aaaaaah!

365
00:23:16,380 --> 00:23:17,540
That's fine by me.

366
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:25,760
So Ryo-chan used a computer to swap
himself in for Kei-chan in the photo

367
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:29,720
I don't know what's going on,
but did it really need to go that far?

368
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:31,280
Well, there's a lot going on, you know.

369
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:34,700
Mother, please help me!

370
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:38,580
They say the more you fight,
the closer you are, right?

371
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:40,640
It's not like that!

372
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:45,100
If I say I won't forgive you,
then I absolutely won't forgive you!

373
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:47,560
Help me!

374
00:23:48,100 --> 00:23:49,440
Hey, wait!

375
00:23:50,020 --> 00:23:52,180
What a truly close pair they are.

376
00:23:53,020 --> 00:23:56,380
You're nothing,
you're nothing, you're nothing!

377
00:23:57,300 --> 00:24:00,920
If we're talking origins, you're the
one who just kept watch, weren't you!

378
00:24:04,220 --> 00:24:06,500
How vexing, how vexing!

379
00:24:06,500 --> 00:24:09,380
The plums I pickled with all my heart.

380
00:24:09,380 --> 00:24:13,220
That man buried them in the ground
without taking a single bite.

381
00:24:13,220 --> 00:24:17,440
Then I'll curse you to the end of time!

382
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:21,340
Next time: The Cursed Pickled Plum Jar,
a curse it is!

383
00:24:35,700 --> 00:24:44,100
Surprise and commotion,
with spirit and resolution, quickly erased

384
00:24:44,100 --> 00:24:55,680
predicted and decided, with flashes of inspiration,
bouncing, gathered together, action, flying away

385
00:24:56,580 --> 00:25:00,820
above all,
the power of being simply yourself

386
00:25:00,820 --> 00:25:06,360
Everyone gather, if you come here

387
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:12,700
like a dream, the final energy

388
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:17,120
gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday

389
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:20,000
paint the universe,
and when you stand on the ground

390
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,860
just like the star of Kameari coming,
it's the same

391
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:27,460
This should be good enough, right?

392
00:25:27,460 --> 00:25:29,000
Like hell it is!

393
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,720
Thank you for watching.

